  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Registration and Identification System 2022/2023 project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Registration and Identification System (NRIS) Project which commenced in November 2016 has enabled the provision of Biometric National IDs to Malawian citizens aged 16 years and above. This flagship national system is outstanding amongst African countries. The project was implemented by National Registration Bureau supported by a UNDP-administered basked fund of over US$ 55 million to which Government of Malawi, UK, EU, Norway, Ireland and USAID contributed. The project&#x2019;s key achievements for 2016/2019 include the impressively successful registration of over 9.9 million Malawians, and the issuing of unique biometric ID smart cards.</narrative>
  </description>
